<title>FRANCE: AGF holds 5.08 pct of Cr National votes.</title>
<headline>AGF holds 5.08 pct of Cr National votes.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-08-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>French insurer AGF holds 5.08 percent of the  voting rights in bank Credit National-Natexis, the CMF markets regulator  said on Friday.</p>
<p>The statement was issued in line with rules requiring notification  when a stake moves above five percent, it said.</p>
<p>An AGF spokesman said the rise in shareholding resulted from a shareholder  pact struck when Credit National bought the BFCE bank from AGF.</p>
<p>The completion of transactions foreseen under that pact should leave  AGF with about seven percent of Credit National.</p>
</text>
